    "body": "@chiefy Thanks, that pretty much clears up the source!\r\n\r\nLooks like https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/context.rs#L586 uses spaces as separators for the pipestatus, but our ZSH script doesn't quote it, resulting in the arguments being split before clap ever sees them.\r\n\r\nI vaguely remember writing a patch that would let starship accept multiple formats of pipestatus, but I don't recall whether this was due to a defect in some shell mechanism or because it seemed most natural with the way that clapv2 parsed arguments.",
